      "Ask the accounts team to name the rule that failed before writing the entry. A rule may be missing, unclear, or simply not followed. Each cause leads to a different fix. An entry without a rule reference becomes a story rather than a control.",
      "Keep the definition visible beside the log so a new specialist can apply it without asking. A short note with two examples is more useful than a long policy. Review the definition when a new work type is added. A definition that drifts creates a log nobody trusts.",
      "## Capture the missing fact and the decision",
