      "If there is no decision, say so and use the space for a trend the owner should know. Do not invent a decision to make the report look important. A short note that the lane is stable is useful. The owner should be able to stop reading after the first line and still know the main point.",
      "Give the owner two options when a decision is needed. State the consequence of each in one line. A recommendation can follow in a separate line. The owner may have context the team does not, so keep the options visible.",
      "Write the decision line in plain language, not in a metric name. A sentence such as approve a second reviewer for the refund lane is clearer than review the approval capacity. The owner should know what action is requested. A vague line invites a vague response.",
      "## Show movement instead of a queue copy",
