      "State the source and the date of the data. A report without a date is hard to trust. If the data is incomplete, say what is missing and how it affects the result. A caveat is better than a false precision.",
      "Avoid a composite score that hides the parts. If a single score is useful, show the components beside it. The owner should be able to see which part moved. A score without the parts invites the wrong fix.",
      "Keep the table to six rows and use the same labels each week. A changing label makes the trend unreadable. If a new measure is needed, replace a less useful row rather than adding another. A stable table is easier to compare.",
      "## Review the report with the owner",
