      "Keep the report to one page. A longer report may be complete but it will not be read every week. Link the detail for the owner who wants it. The weekly habit depends on a short, consistent format.",
      "Review the format after a month and remove any field that never changed a decision. Add a field only when the owner asks for it. A report that grows without review becomes a chore. The goal is a five-minute read that leads to one clear action.",
      "Send the report before the meeting, not during it. The owner can read it in advance and bring a decision. A report presented for the first time in the meeting is usually discussed line by line. Advance reading saves time."
